default = []`) | `cargo check --no-default-features` / `cargo test --no-default-features` |\n\n  Both are exercised by `scripts/verify_all.sh`.\n\n## Runtime configuration axes actually branched on by the C\n\n| axis | values the C distinguishes |\n|---|---|\n| entry point | `main` (process, reads stdin) — `run(int)` (exported, callable directly any number of times) |\n| accumulated global state | `the_house.floors` (+1 per `run`), `.bathrooms` (+1.0 per `run`), `.bedrooms` (+`extra` per `run`) → the Nth call prints different values |\n| `scanf` whitespace prefix | none / `' '` / `'\\t'` / `'\\n'` / `'\\v'` / `'\\f'` / `'\\r'` / long mixed run (crosses the 4096-byte stdio buffer) |\n| `scanf` sign | absent / `'+'` / `'-'` |\n| `scanf` digit run | 1 digit / many digits / leading zeros / ≥19 digits (long-overflow path) |\n| `scanf` terminator | EOF / newline / space / non-digit garbage / second token |\n| `x` value class | `0` / positive small / negative small / `INT_MAX` / `INT_MIN` / wraps `bedrooms` |\n| stdout kind | pipe (fully buffered in C) / regular file / `/dev/null` |\n| argv | absent / present (ignored by `int main()`) |\n\n## Configuration rows (every combination the C treats differently)\n\nLegend: **P** = process-level differential test (`tests/differential_process.rs`,\nC `build/driver` vs Rust `target/*/driver`, byte-compare stdout+stderr+status),\n**F** = FFI differential test (`tests/differential_ffi.rs`, `libcdriver.so` vs\n`libdriver.so` loaded with `libloading`, byte-compare captured stdout).\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|----|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1  | `main` (P) | stdin `\"0\\n\"` — baseline, `x = 0` | [x] |\n| 2  | `main` (P) | stdin `\"3\\n\"` — small positive | [x] |\n| 3  | `main` (P) | stdin `\"-4\\n\"` — small negative | [x] |\n| 4  | `main` (P) | stdin `\"+7\\n\"` — explicit plus sign | [x] |\n| 5  | `main` (P) | no trailing newline (`\"3\"`, EOF right after the digits) | [x] |\n| 6  | `main` (P) | `\"\\r\\n\"`-terminated (`\"3\\r\\n\"`) | [x] |\n| 7  | `main` (P) | each whitespace kind as prefix: `' '`, `'\\t'`, `'\\n'`, `'\\v'`, `'\\f'`, `'\\r'`, and mixes | [x] |\n| 8  | `main` (P) | >4096 bytes of leading whitespace, then the number (stdio buffer refill) | [x] |\n| 9  | `main` (P) | leading zeros (`\"007\"`), 1..25-digit runs (randomized lengths) | [x] |\n| 10 | `main` (P) | trailing garbage after the number (`\"5abc\"`, `\"5.5\"`, `\"5,\"`) | [x] |\n| 11 | `main` (P) | several tokens (`\"1 2 3\\n\"`, `\"1\\n2\\n\"`) — only the first is read | [x] |\n| 12 | `main` (P) | `INT_MAX`, `INT_MAX-1`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1` exactly | [x] |\n| 13 | `main` (P) | out-of-`int` but in-`long`, out-of-`long`, `2^32`, `2^31`, `LONG_MAX`, `LONG_MIN` | [x] |\n| 14 | `main` (P) | randomized `i32` values (fixed seed, 400 cases) formatted decimal, with random sign form / whitespace / terminator | [x] |\n| 15 | `main` (P) | randomized junk / mixed byte strings (fixed seed, 300 cases, incl. NUL and high bytes) | [x] |\n| 16 | `main` (P) | stdout → regular file instead of pipe (C switches from line to full buffering) | [x] |\n| 17 | `main` (P) | stdout → `/dev/null` | [x] |\n| 18 | `main` (P) | extra argv entries (`driver a b c`) with an otherwise normal stdin | [x] |\n| 19 | `main` (P) | 1 MiB of leading whitespace + number (large stream, many refills) | [x] |\n| 20 | `run` (F) | `run(0)` as the very first call — pristine global state | [x] |\n| 21 | `run` (F) | `run(v)` repeated 200× with randomized `v` (fixed seed) — floors/bathrooms/bedrooms accumulation compared step by step | [x] |\n| 22 | `run` (F) | `run(INT_MAX)` / `run(INT_MIN)` / `run(-1)` / `run(1)` in sequence — wrap-around accumulation | [x] |\n| 23 | `run` (F) | long run of `run(1)` so `bathrooms` grows well past 100.5 (`%.1f` of larger magnitudes) | [x] |\n| 24 | `run` (F) | `run` after `run`: proves the mutated `static`/`static mut` state matches between 